  private handleCredentialError(error: any): void {
    if (error.message?.includes("ManagedIdentityCredential")) {
      console.error(`
⚠️  MANAGED IDENTITY NOT AVAILABLE

Possible causes:
1. Not running on an Azure resource that supports managed identity
2. Managed identity not enabled on the resource
3. User-assigned identity not attached to the resource

Fixes:
- Enable system-assigned identity: Azure Portal → Resource → Identity → System assigned: ON
- Attach user-assigned identity: Azure Portal → Resource → Identity → User assigned → Add
- For local development: az login
